    "lawCode": "Amd §§17-0809 & 17-1909, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5022\n\nSPONSOR: GAUGHRAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nlimiting the exceptions to certain effluent limitations in Nassau and\nSuffolk counties and requiring certain eligible projects for state aid\ninvolving water pollution control revolving fund agreements to take\ncounty-wide or regional wastewater planning into consideration when\ndetermining eligibility\n\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nlimiting the exceptions to certain effluent limitations in Nassau and\nSuffolk counties and requiring certain eligible projects for state aid\ninvolving water pollution control revolving fund agreements to take\ncounty-wide or regional wastewater planning into consideration when\ndetermining eligibility\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA QF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to protect LI water quality.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would eliminate exceptions to certain effluent limitations in\nNassau and Suffolk counties and require that the best available technol-\nogy be used in such counties to reduce nitrogen pollution and that coun-\nty-wide or regional wastewater planning be considered for such adverse\nenvironmental impacts.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nLong Island is blessed with beautiful ocean harbors and good quality\ndrinking water, all of which is derived from sole-source aquifers. As\nmore becomes known about the adverse impacts of Nitrogen on water quali-\nty, additional steps need to be taken to protect these important water\nresources. This legislation will help advance that goal by requiring the\nusage of best available technology and encouraging greater coordination\nof wastewater planning in order to minimize potentially duplicative\ninfrastructure.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS6384 of 2019/2020: Referred to Environmental Conservation\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
